## 6. 5-Minute-Native Bar Counter

Confirms the design already in Architecture v1.0 §4, with one added implementation
constraint: the counter must be incremented in the **outer, stateful script context**, once
per confirmed 5-minute bar as detected per §3 (Case B) or §4 (Case C) — never inside a
security() expression, for the same side-effect reason as everything else in this report.
For Case A (chart = 5m exactly), the counter can either mirror chart-native `bar_index`
directly (since the two are already identical in that case) or route through the same
detection mechanism as B/C for implementation uniformity — a design choice with no
correctness implications either way, worth deciding for code-simplicity reasons rather than
technical necessity.

`POOL_EXPIRY_BARS = 200`, `POI_EXPIRY_BARS = 150`, `M9_CANDIDATE_EXPIRY_BARS = 150`,
`M10_REC_EXPIRY_BARS = 100` remain exactly as-is, per Architecture v1.0 §4 — nothing in this
feasibility pass changes that conclusion.

