## 9. Can M5–M9 Function Bodies Remain Unchanged?

**No, not entirely — but the exceptions are narrow and enumerated.** Per §5: the pivot
detection and ATR calculation in `f_m5_update_structure`, and the 2–3 bar historical offsets
in M7's FVG/OB pattern detection, must be refactored from implicit series operators to
explicit buffer-based computation. Every other M5–M9 function that operates on
already-computed state (structure fields, pool/POI/candidate objects) rather than raw series
requires only a parameter-source substitution (5m-fetched OHLC/counter instead of bare
chart-native series), not a logic change.

