## §2. Corrected Boundary and Layering

Architecture v1.0's single "Data Layer → M5" boundary is replaced with four explicit
sub-responsibilities, each independently identified in the task requirements:

```
[1] 5-minute data acquisition           (NEW DATA-LAYER RESPONSIBILITY — §3, §4)
        │
        ▼
[2] 5-minute historical buffering       (NEW DATA-LAYER RESPONSIBILITY — §6)
        │
        ▼
[3] 5-minute bar confirmation/dedup     (NEW DATA-LAYER RESPONSIBILITY — §7)
        │
        ▼
[4] Stateful M5→M10 execution           (EXISTING PIPELINE — REFACTOR where noted, §8–§10)
```

**[1] 5-minute data acquisition** happens *inside* a `request.security*()` expression — the
only context in which genuinely 5-minute-native series data (as opposed to chart-native
data) can be read. This step returns data only; it performs no mutation and calls no
M5–M10 function.

**[2] 5-minute historical buffering** happens in the **outer, stateful script context**,
immediately after acquisition. This is where the manually maintained OHLC ring buffer
(§6) is updated — one update per confirmed 5-minute bar. This step is what makes
`close[1]`, `high[2]`, `ta.pivothigh`, and `ta.atr` reproducible outside of Pine's native
series machinery (§6).

**[3] 5-minute bar confirmation/deduplication** also happens in the outer, stateful
context, gating whether step [4] runs at all on a given script execution (§7).

**[4] Stateful M5→M10 execution** is the existing pipeline, invoked once per confirmed
5-minute bar (or, on chart timeframes above 5m, once per contained 5-minute bar, in
chronological order — §5 of v1.0, carried forward unchanged). This is where M5–M10's
registry mutations occur, entirely outside any security expression.

**Correction to v1.0's boundary statement:** "M5's input boundary changes from the chart's
bare series to this tuple, and nothing past that handoff point changes" is only true for
the subset of M5–M9 operations enumerated in §8 below as **[UNCHANGED EXISTING LOGIC]**. A
named, narrow subset requires **[REQUIRED M5–M9 REFACTOR]** (§8). Both facts now hold
simultaneously; v1.0 asserted only the first.

