## §5. Data Acquisition — Chart Timeframe = 5m (Case A) — [NEW DATA-LAYER RESPONSIBILITY, degenerate case]

One chart-native confirmed bar is one 5-minute bar. No lower/higher-timeframe fetch is
structurally required, but for implementation uniformity the Data Layer may route Case A
through the same confirmation/dedup mechanism as B/C (§7) rather than special-casing it.
This is a code-simplicity choice with **no correctness implications either way** — carried
forward unchanged from v1.0 §6.

Case A is also the basis for the buffer-vs-native parity test (§9 test 2/3), since it is
the one case where the manually maintained buffer (§6) and Pine's native series machinery
can be run side-by-side on identical bars.

