## 5. Historical Series Operations on 5-Minute Bars

This is the part of the source that cannot survive unchanged, and it is larger than a
casual read of Architecture v1.0 suggests.

Pine's `[]` history operator and `ta.*` built-ins operate on native Pine series maintained
by the runtime within one of exactly two contexts: the main script's own chart-native bar
sequence, or the isolated, side-effect-free context inside a `request.security*()`
expression. No context is both genuinely 5-minute-native and able to mutate persistent
registries — so these operations must be reimplemented against a **manually maintained,
Data-Layer-owned rolling buffer** of the last several 5-minute bars' OHLC, updated once per
confirmed 5-minute bar in the outer stateful context.

**Confirmed source locations requiring reimplementation (not approximation):**

| Source construct | Found in | Definitional semantics preserved | Reproduction |
|---|---|---|---|
| `ta.pivothigh(high, SWING_LOOKBACK, SWING_LOOKBACK)` / `ta.pivotlow(low, ...)` | `f_m5_update_structure` | A pivot high/low is the max/min value within a centered `2·SWING_LOOKBACK+1`-bar window. | Explicit windowed-extremum comparison over the manual buffer's high/low column, same `SWING_LOOKBACK`. |
| `ta.atr(ATR_LENGTH)` | `f_m5_update_structure` (`st.current_context.atr := ta.atr(ATR_LENGTH)`) | Wilder's RMA-smoothed true range. | `var float` running ATR, updated once per confirmed 5m bar via the buffer's true-range value, same `ATR_LENGTH`. |
| `close[1]` | `f_m5_update_structure` (bull/bear break detection) | Prior bar's close, in the series' own native timeframe. | Buffer offset-1 read, buffer being 5m-native by construction. |
| `close[1]`, `open[1]`, `high[2]`, `low[2]` | `f_m7_update_fvgs` (bull/bear FVG detection, and gap top/bottom calc) | 2–3 bar historical offsets. | Buffer offsets. |
| `close[1]`, `open[1]`, `close[2]`, `open[2]`, `high[1]`, `low[1]` | `f_m7_update_obs` (bull/bear OB detection) | Same. | Buffer offsets. |

**Formula/threshold preservation constraint:** in every row above, only the *data source*
changes — from Pine's implicit series machinery to an explicit buffer. `SWING_LOOKBACK`,
`ATR_LENGTH`, and every comparison operator remain byte-identical.

