## 7. Preventing Duplicate 5m Processing

- **Case A (chart = 5m):** trivial — one chart-native confirmed bar is one 5m bar.
- **Case B (chart > 5m):** resolved by the §3 rule — the lower-timeframe array is fetched
  only on outer-bar confirmation, so there is no risk of processing a still-forming
  intrabar, and `request.security_lower_tf()` does not re-return already-processed
  intrabars from a prior chart bar (documented behavior).
- **Case C (chart < 5m):** the §4 timestamp-change detection, gated on outer-bar
  confirmation, fires at most once per genuinely new 5m close by construction.

