## Pre-v1.3 Technical Analysis — NOT an Architecture Document, NOT Frozen

Status: **INVESTIGATION ONLY.** No Pine code. No architecture changes yet. No freeze. This
resolves the one open question standing between Technical Feasibility Report v2 and
Architecture v1.3: whether Case B (chart timeframe above 5m) can process a closed 5-minute
intrabar as soon as it closes, or must wait for the enclosing chart bar to confirm.

**Direct answer up front, expanded below:** No — not in the sense your question is really
asking (durable, registry-committing processing of a closed 5m intrabar before the outer bar
confirms). The reason is Pine's **realtime rollback mechanism**, which is a documented,
non-optional property of how `var`-scoped state behaves during a forming bar — not a
convention or a stylistic choice you could code around. Design A (outer-bar confirmation) is
not merely the safer of two viable options; it is the only one of the two that can produce a
durable, replay-consistent result. There is, however, a narrow and useful middle ground
(§6) that gets you *early visibility* without claiming *early commitment* — worth folding
into v1.3 as an optional addition, not a replacement of the Design A rule already adopted.

