## §5. Case A — Chart Timeframe = 5 Minutes

One chart-native confirmed bar is one 5-minute bar. No lower/higher-timeframe fetch is
structurally required; for implementation uniformity the Data Layer may route Case A through
the same confirmation/dedup mechanism as B/C (§11), or may mirror chart-native `bar_index`
directly for the execution counter (§10) — a code-simplicity choice with no correctness
difference either way. Case A is also the basis for the buffer-vs-native parity tests
(§13, tests 2–3), since it is the one case where the manually maintained buffer (§9) and
Pine's native series machinery can be compared directly on identical bars.

