## §10. 5-Minute-Native Execution Counter

- A new counter, owned by the Data Layer, replaces bare `bar_index` for every M5–M10
  sequencing/expiry use identified in §7–§8.
- Increments by exactly 1 per **processed confirmed 5-minute bar** — never per chart bar,
  and never inside a `request.security*()` expression.
- **`POOL_EXPIRY_BARS = 200`, `POI_EXPIRY_BARS = 150`, `M9_CANDIDATE_EXPIRY_BARS = 150`, and
  `M10_REC_EXPIRY_BARS = 100` are not changed.** Only their timebase changes — from
  chart-native bars (a chart-timeframe-dependent number of minutes) to 5-minute execution
  bars (always 500 minutes for the 100-bar constant, on every chart display timeframe).
- For Case A, the counter may mirror chart-native `bar_index` directly, or route through the
  same detection mechanism as Cases B/C — a code-simplicity choice with no correctness
  difference (§5).

