## §2. Why the Original Scalar-Tuple Design Is Not Achievable — unchanged from v1.3

Pine enforces, at the compiler level, that the expression argument to
`request.security()`/`request.security_lower_tf()` must have no side effects. M5–M10's
side-effecting operations (`array.push`, `table.cell`, `field := value` mutation of shared
registries) cannot occur inside a security expression. This is why the four-stage layering
in §1 is required, not optional.

