## §3. Case B — Final Execution Decision — unchanged from v1.3

**Design A — outer-bar confirmation — remains the only durable execution model for Case B
(chart timeframe strictly above 5 minutes).**

```
request.security_lower_tf()
          ↓
wait for outer chart-bar confirmation (barstate.isconfirmed on the outer bar)
          ↓
retrieve all contained 5m bars
          ↓
process chronologically
          ↓
exactly one M5→M10 pass per confirmed 5m bar
```

This remains deliberately not 5-minute-equivalent realtime latency on a higher-timeframe
chart. The architecture prioritizes deterministic committed state over latency — a stated
tradeoff, not an incidental limitation. This decision is final per the review: "Design A
should remain the frozen candidate."

