## §9. Manual 5-Minute History Buffer — CORRECTED (Correction 1, the most significant)

**v1.3's buffer-depth requirement was wrong and is replaced.**

v1.3 stated the minimum buffer depth as `max(SWING_LOOKBACK, ATR_LENGTH, 3)`. This is
incorrect for the pivot calculation specifically. `ta.pivothigh`/`ta.pivotlow` with
`leftbars = rightbars = L` require `L` bars on **each side** of the candidate bar, plus the
candidate bar itself, to confirm a pivot — a centered window of `2L + 1` bars, not `L` bars.
Per current documentation, a pivot is only confirmed once the right-side bars exist, meaning
the confirmation is itself delayed by `L` bars relative to the candidate. With
`SWING_LOOKBACK = 5` (the script's current default), v1.3's stated depth of 5 entries falls
five bars short of the 11 bars actually required.

**Corrected buffer-depth requirement:**

> The minimum buffer depth must be sufficient for the largest required centered pivot
> window — **`2 × SWING_LOOKBACK + 1`** — plus whatever additional history is required by
> ATR initialization and the largest historical offset in use (`max(high[2], low[2])` →
> depth ≥ 3). **The exact final depth is not frozen by this document** until the ATR
> initialization requirement is resolved — see the open item below, carried through
> unchanged from the reasoning that flagged it as unresolved in Architecture v1.2/v1.3.

**Required buffer contents (corrected):** a fixed-length rolling window of 5-minute
`(open, high, low, close, true_range)` tuples, sized to at least
`max(2 × SWING_LOOKBACK + 1, <ATR-initialization-dependent depth, still open>, 3)` entries,
plus one running-ATR state value.

**Operations the buffer must reproduce, without approximating their semantics — unchanged
from v1.3:**

| Operation | Definitional semantics to preserve | Reproduction approach |
|---|---|---|
| `ta.pivothigh(high, L, L)` / `ta.pivotlow(low, L, L)` | The bar `L` positions back is a pivot iff it is the max/min value within the centered `2L+1`-bar window around it; confirmation itself lags the candidate bar by `L` bars. | Explicit windowed-extremum comparison over the buffer's high/low column, buffer depth ≥ `2L+1`, same `L` (`SWING_LOOKBACK`). |
| `ta.atr(ATR_LENGTH)` | Wilder's RMA-smoothed true range. | Running ATR state, updated per confirmed 5m bar from the buffer's true-range value, same `ATR_LENGTH`. |
| `close[1]`, `open[1]` | Prior bar's close/open, native timeframe. | Buffer offset-1 read. |
| `high[2]`, `low[2]` | Two bars back, native timeframe. | Buffer offset-2 read. |

**Formula/threshold preservation constraint — unchanged:** only the data source changes;
`SWING_LOOKBACK`, `ATR_LENGTH`, and every comparison operator remain byte-identical to the
current source.

**[OPEN VERIFICATION REQUIRED] — unchanged in substance from v1.3, restated with the
corrected buffer-depth dependency made explicit:**

- Exact initialization/seeding behavior of `ta.atr()`'s underlying RMA smoothing on the very
  first bars of a series — **this directly determines the final frozen buffer depth**,
  which is why depth is not frozen in this document.
- Exact `na` propagation behavior of `ta.pivothigh`/`ta.pivotlow` during the first `L` bars
  of a series, before a full centered window is available.
- Tie-breaking behavior of `ta.pivothigh`/`ta.pivotlow` when multiple bars within the window
  share the identical extreme value.
- Insufficient-history behavior for buffer-based historical offsets before the buffer has
  accumulated enough bars (now including the corrected `2L+1` pivot-window requirement, not
  just the `close[1]`/`high[2]`-level offsets).

