## §9. Manual 5-Minute History Buffer — Precision Correction (does not change the §9
## conclusion from v1.4, refines how it is stated)

The `2 × SWING_LOOKBACK + 1` centered-window depth requirement from v1.4 is unchanged and
correct. Two precisions are added, per review:

**Precision 1 — windowed-extremum reproduction is necessary but not sufficient.** A buffer
depth of `2L + 1` is what makes it *possible* to compute "is this the highest/lowest value in
the centered window" — but that computation alone is not automatically identical to
`ta.pivothigh()`/`ta.pivotlow()`'s actual behavior in every case. Genuine Pine pivot
semantics include additional behavior beyond a plain windowed maximum/minimum comparison —
specifically, `na`-handling before a full window exists, confirmation timing (a pivot at bar
`N` is only knowable once bar `N+L` has occurred), and tie-breaking when multiple bars share
the identical extreme value. **The buffer-depth correction (`2L+1`) is necessary for
reproduction to be possible at all; it does not by itself establish that the reproduction is
correct.** The acceptance test for pivot parity (§13, test 3) is expanded accordingly, below.

**Precision 2 — decoupling the ATR open item from the architecture freeze.** v1.4 stated
that the ATR-seeding open item "directly determines the final frozen buffer depth" and left
the exact depth unfrozen as a consequence. This is corrected to avoid holding the entire
architecture hostage to one implementation-time constant:

> **The architecture freeze establishes the requirement:**
> `BUFFER_DEPTH >= max(2 × SWING_LOOKBACK + 1, ATR_REQUIRED_HISTORY, 3)`, where
> `ATR_REQUIRED_HISTORY` is a named, currently-unresolved quantity — **not** a blocker to
> freezing this requirement itself. **The implementation freeze**, a separate and later step,
> determines the exact numeric value of `ATR_REQUIRED_HISTORY` once Pine's `ta.atr()` RMA
> seeding behavior is verified, and sets the buffer's concrete allocated depth accordingly.
> The architectural requirement above is freeze-ready as stated; only the numeric
> instantiation of one of its terms is deferred to implementation-time verification.

**Operations the buffer must reproduce — unchanged from v1.4:**

| Operation | Definitional semantics to preserve | Reproduction approach |
|---|---|---|
| `ta.pivothigh(high, L, L)` / `ta.pivotlow(low, L, L)` | Centered `2L+1`-bar window extremum, confirmed only once the right-side `L` bars exist, with defined `na` and tie-break behavior (§13 test 3). | Windowed-extremum comparison over the buffer, depth ≥ `2L+1`, same `L`. |
| `ta.atr(ATR_LENGTH)` | Wilder's RMA-smoothed true range. | Running ATR state, `BUFFER_DEPTH >= ATR_REQUIRED_HISTORY` per the corrected requirement above. |
| `close[1]`, `open[1]` | Prior bar, native timeframe. | Buffer offset-1 read. |
| `high[2]`, `low[2]` | Two bars back, native timeframe. | Buffer offset-2 read. |

**[OPEN VERIFICATION REQUIRED] — unchanged in substance, now explicitly decoupled from
architecture freeze per Precision 2:**

- `ta.atr()`'s exact RMA seeding/initialization behavior — determines `ATR_REQUIRED_HISTORY`
