stated explicitly because an unscoped reading of the rule above could be misapplied to halt
M9/M10 processing entirely during buffer recovery — which this document does not intend and
explicitly prohibits:

> **The buffer-invalidation rule applies only to M5's historical-structure calculations**
> that depend on the buffer — swing/pivot detection, ATR maintenance, and M7's FVG/OB
> historical-offset detection. **It does not apply to, and must not be implemented in a way
> that suspends, M9/M10 lifecycle processing of already-existing candidates and
> recommendations.** Trigger/lifecycle resolution (`f_m9_evaluate_lifecycle`,
> `f_m10_stage5_lifecycle`) reads current-bar high/low and the execution counter directly,
