## §13. Acceptance Tests — Corrected (Tests 8, 14, 15 revised; Test 17 added)

### Primary parity test — unchanged from v1.5

### Mandatory implementation-level tests

Tests 1–7, 9–13, 16 unchanged from v1.5. Tests 8, 14, and 15 are revised below; a new test
17 is added.

**8. Expiry timing — CORRECTED, replacing the unconditional version:**

> Confirm that, **under continuous accessible 5-minute data**, `POOL_EXPIRY_BARS`,
> `POI_EXPIRY_BARS`, `M9_CANDIDATE_EXPIRY_BARS`, and `M10_REC_EXPIRY_BARS` expire at the
> same fixed wall-clock offset regardless of chart display timeframe. **Separately**,
> confirm that for a recommendation/candidate/POI/pool whose lifecycle spans a
> classified unavailable-data gap (§6), expiry is measured correctly against the
> **processed-bar counter** (§10) — not fabricated wall-clock minutes — and that no
> synthetic counter increments occur for the unavailable interval. A gap-spanning lifecycle
> not matching a naively-computed wall-clock offset is expected behavior, not a test
> failure, per §10's corrected contract.

**14. Partial-intrabar-availability test (Case B) — CORRECTED, replacing the four-way
version:**

> On a chart bar where fewer than the expected number of 5-minute intrabars is returned,
> confirm the Data Layer: detects the shortfall; classifies it as session-related absence
> only where determinable from session boundaries; otherwise records it as an unknown/
> unclassified data-availability condition rather than asserting a specific cause (§6); and
> never fabricates a missing bar under any classification.

**15. Case C confirmed-retrieval correctness test — CORRECTED, replacing the realtime/
historical-equality version:**

> Confirm that the offset-expression + `lookahead_on` retrieval mechanism (§6) correctly
> retrieves the confirmed preceding 5-minute bar, and that — given identical underlying
> 5-minute OHLC/time input — its retrieved values match the corresponding native 5-minute
> bar. Validate the mechanism **independently** in historical replay and in realtime
> execution. **Do not require realtime-fetched input to equal subsequently-retrieved
> historical input** — per §12 guarantee 3, that equivalence is not architecturally
> guaranteed. Any divergence attributable to documented feed/provider behavior is not, by
> itself, a test failure.

**17. New — Case C gap buffer-invalidation and lifecycle-continuity test:**

> Construct or identify a historical period containing a classified unavailable-data gap on
> a 1m/3m chart (§6). Confirm: (a) the buffer does not treat the pre-gap and post-gap bars
> as adjacent — no spurious true-range/pivot/offset corruption at the gap boundary; (b) M5's
> new-structure detection (swing/pivot/FVG/OB) is suspended until contiguous post-gap
> history satisfies §9's depth requirement; and (c) any candidate or recommendation that
> existed before the gap continues to be evaluated for trigger/SL/TP/expiry against valid
> current-bar inputs throughout the gap, per §6's explicit lifecycle-continuity carve-out —
> confirming the buffer-invalidation rule does not suspend M9/M10 processing.

